Z||000010||Fierokid87||12-26-2001||04:57 PM||||I like the way you have the exaust wrap.  I wonder how well that will work.  Does anyone think it is a good allternative to the stock heat shelds?<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="red"> Fierokid's  Web site:</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="white">http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero</FONT><P><FONT COLOR="blue">AIM: Fierokid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid</FONT><P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierokid.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Neal||12-27-2001||12:14 AM||||got some more pics for everyone<P>Here is a quick shot of the alfa spyder engine bay.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/alfa_motor.jpg"> <P>Back to todays work, to clear the 3.4 pan the motor mount bracket had to be notched.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/notch_2.jpg"> <P>It looks like the transmission had a clutch explode along the way  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/bellhousing_broken.jpg"> <P>Not the best solution, but it will do.  Overnight epoxy and 10 minutes to apply  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Im hoping it will do its job.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/bellhousing_fix.jpg"> <P>Ive got lots more pics but i dont wanna make this totally inaccessable to dial-ups.<BR>The motor is now all preped and ready to go in the car, from the top :WTF:<BR>Im going to try it this way, everything came out through the top, just piece by piece.  Last motor i did by dropping the cradle, so soon ill say which is better/easier.<P>stay tuned||||reg||1
Z||000012||G-Nasty||12-27-2001||04:17 AM||||May need Headers w/ 2030. I used this compucam on my first rebuild. If you got valve lash correct 1/4 to 1/2 turn and use thread lock on all critical bolts and proper timing you should be in the clear. White will be my next rebuild color. ||||reg||1
Z||000013||FormulaJoe||12-27-2001||10:57 AM||||Did you do the finish on your valve covers yourself?  I have always liked wrinkle finish, on somethings.  Would like to put it on a couple things I have.  I noticed that the Alfa has that wrap on its exhaust, does it work good and keep its looks?  Was thinking of doing something like that on my exhaust when I get it made, since there will be no factory heat shielding for it and I want to keep temps in control as much as possiable.  That engine looks nice by the way, dont you just love the way a new engine looks, inside as well as outside?<P>------------------<BR>Yellow Formula<BR>(soon to be 3.4 DOHC)||||reg||6
